Z||000000||WKDFIRO||08-29-2000||10:30 PM|||| <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=422567108&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=422567108&r=0&t=0</A> <P>"Make your Fiero 2M4 scream past those 2M6's and GT's!"<P>I just wanted to clarify the quote above found on the ebay site. The headers alone will NOT make your 4 cyl Fiero scream past much of anything near the 2M6 and GTs. <P>When I had my 87 four cyl I felt that it was THE best thing you could do for the 4 cyl. The stock exhaust on it is a sad and almost choking especially if you put them together.  Best I could do was to amaze my friends that I could keep up with them. On long trips though it sure was nice to be only topping off the tank when the GTs and 2M6s were filing up!!!<P>Tri-Ys are great! It really open up the power, but don't expect miracles... just enjoy the gas mileage.<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000001||theogre||08-29-2000||11:13 PM||||4703 bolted to the 87 head? or did it need something added. Hooker says it doesn't fit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||08-31-2000||05:01 PM||||Unless there is a specific header for the 87 that I was not aware of there should be no reason for it not to fit all of them. We added nothing to the header. Though I have stated many times that the pipe does come very close to the starter solenoid. <P>Might that be what they mean? I can't see how, the blocks are identical in the exhaust port and starter configurations. Hmmmmmmmm.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-01-2000||12:30 PM||||I can't see any differance either. All I know is what hooker told me. That's why I posted asking if anyone had one on an 87-88 a few weeks ago. I know the intakes won't interchange, I couldn't find any info on the exhuast pattern on the heads. (The manifolds list as not interchanging. Mostly because the 87+ doesn't use the heat duct to the air cleaner.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phantom Rage||09-02-2000||10:58 AM|||| I don't know if the tri-y hooker header will work on an 87-88.  I do know the 4 into 1 Hooker Super Competition will work on an 88. The 4 into 1 are not nearly as close to the starter as the tri-y design.  The main problem with the 4 into 1 is that it leaves no room for a cat, in the original location. <P>P.S.  Besides the porblem with no cat, a bunghole will also be needed.  Provision's to hook up a 3-inch exhaust pipe to its 3-inch collector will also have to be made.  The bottom line is, this sucker is not designed for street use.<P>||||reg||7
